    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Yes, standard homeowners insurance policies in Utah typically cover hail damage. Damage to your roof, siding, windows, and outdoor structures caused by a hailstorm falls under your policy's dwelling or other structures coverage, minus the cost of your deductible.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What is Covered"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roofing: Cracked, bruised, or punctured shingles, as well as damaged vents and flashing."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Exterior:\nDented or cracked siding, broken windows, and damaged gutters."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Other Structures: Detached garages, sheds, and fences on your property."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Personal Property:\nBelongings damaged if a severe hailstorm breaches your home's exterior (like a roof leak ruining interior furniture)."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          4,
          5,
          6
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Important Policy Details to Check"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Deductibles: Some Utah policies enforce a separate, higher deductible specifically for wind and hail damage rather than your standard all-peril deductible."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cosmetic Exclusions: Certain insurers exclude purely cosmetic dents (such as minor siding or metal roof dings) if the hail does not compromise the functional integrity of the material.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Maintenance Limits: Pre-existing wear and tear or a heavily neglected roof can result in a claim denial."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "You can review state guidelines and consumer tips through the Utah Insurance Department\n\n.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
            "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          9,
          10
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your insurance provider"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Whether you are looking at a specific deductible amount for wind/hail"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you figure out if filing a claim makes financial sense for your situation."
      }
    ],
